{"time":{"created":1791460821256,"streamed":1791460934221,"completed":1791460934254},"agent":"build","model":{"id":"nemotron-3-ultra-free","providerID":"opencode","variant":"default"},"content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user is pointing out that according to the brief, a game can win before the slide phase too - if a player gets 3 in a row during placement, they should win. But my DESIGN.md explicitly says "Win checked during placement? No — only after slides (simpler, avoids premature wins)."

The brief says: "Design and build a two-player tic-tac-toe variant in which a game can never end in a draw." It doesn't explicitly forbid wins during placement. The user is suggesting that if someone gets 3 in a row during placement, they should win immediately.

